Changes in robCompositions version 2.7.0
  + aDist() gains new options (defaults unchanged):
    - type = "rows" returns the distance for each pair of corresponding rows,
      type = "cross" the matrix of distances between all rows of x and all rows
      of y (y may have any number of rows).
    - weights: weighted Aitchison distance (part weights via a change of the
      reference measure, Egozcue and Pawlowsky-Glahn 2016); unit weights give
      the ordinary Aitchison distance.
    - na.rm = TRUE: missing, zero and negative cells are left out and the
      distance is computed from the available pairwise log-ratios, scaled to
      all log-ratios (Gower-type).
    - cellweights: non-negative cell weights, e.g. from a cellwise-robust
      method; na.rm is the special case of weights 0 and 1.
  + aDist() is now computed from clr coordinates in R instead of C: 25 to 100
    times faster for larger data, same results up to rounding (relative
    differences around 1e-16). The C routine has been removed.
  + aDist(x, y) now stops with an informative error for missing or infinite
    values (before, a generic error from the C call). Distances involving rows
    with zero or negative values are NaN, now with a warning that points to
    na.rm = TRUE (before, NaN or Inf without a warning).
  + aDist(x) for a single data set, without weights, cellweights and na.rm, is
    unchanged: dist(cenLR(x)$x.clr), which tolerates missing cells (and is
    used by clustCoDa(distMethod = "Aitchison")).
  + the weighted distance matrix (y = NULL) is computed in one vectorised step
    from the weighted clr coordinates.
  + new function aDistDens() for the Aitchison distance between densities in
    the Bayes space, optionally with respect to a reference measure P.

Changes in robCompositions version 2.6.1
  + src/zeros.cpp now includes <cassert> explicitly, needed to build against
    Eigen 5.0.1 (RcppEigen). Thanks to Dirk Eddelbuettel.
  + trapzc() returned a wrong value for a grid of only two points (the end
    points were counted twice); results for three or more points are unchanged.
    It now stops with an error for fewer than two points.
  + the help pages of fcenLR(), fcenLRp(), fcenLRu(), fcenLRinv() and trapzc()
    have been rewritten: defining formulas, input requirements (equidistant
    grid, strictly positive density), correct return values, cross-references,
    and examples that no longer refer to an undefined object (t.fine).
  + new tests for the functional clr transformations.
  + aDist(x, y), and hence ced(), now stops with an error if x and y do not have
    the same dimensions. Before, a different number of columns silently gave a
    wrong distance, and fewer rows in y made the C code read beyond the data.
    Results for valid input are unchanged. The registration of the internal C
    routine has been corrected (a misspelled NAOK argument was passed on to it).
  + the help page of ced() has been rewritten (definition, input requirements,
    return value, DOIs) and tests for aDist() and ced() have been added.
  + the imputation vignette no longer links to a report on a retired web page
    of the Swiss Federal Statistical Office (the URL now returns 404).

Changes in robCompositions version 2.6.0
  + new function cellNetCoDa() for cellwise-robust network (Gaussian graphical
    model) estimation of compositional data, with print/summary/plot methods.
    Cellwise outliers are detected and down-weighted before a sparse graph is
    estimated by neighbourhood selection ("mb") or the graphical lasso on the
    clr covariance ("glasso"); the penalty is chosen by StARS.
  + imputeBDLs() has been renamed to imputeBDL(). imputeBDLs() is kept as a
    deprecated alias and will be removed in a future release.
  + impRZilr() is deprecated and is now an alias of imputeBDL() (the same method:
    EM-based replacement of rounded zeros in pivot coordinates). Its results are
    unchanged; please switch to imputeBDL().
  + imputeBDL() now correctly imputes values below the detection limit even when
    they are supplied as small positive numbers rather than exact zeros. Earlier
    imputeBDLs() silently skipped such values because the checkData() thresholding
    result was discarded. Results for the documented usage (rounded zeros pre-coded
    as 0) are unchanged.
  + impAll() no longer returns NULL for data containing rounded zeros (it read a
    list element that no longer exists); it now calls imputeBDL() internally.
  + removed a stray diagnostic print() from the rounded-zero imputation, a
    duplicate internal impAll() definition, and broken non-default code paths
    (the 'test' argument of imputeBDLs() and the unused 'variation' branch of
    impRZilr()).
  + imputeUDLs() now returns an object of class "replaced", and the imputed-zero
    index ('wind') of imputeBDL()/imputeUDLs() is returned aligned with the
    original column order.

Changes in robCompositions version 2.5.0
  + new function cellPcaCoDa() for cellwise-robust PCA of compositional data,
    with print/summary/plot methods, implementing Templ (2026, Advances in
    Data Analysis and Classification)
  + new function contaminate_simplex() to generate cellwise-contaminated
    compositions
  + cellPcaCoDa() defaults now follow the paper: Tukey biweight loss and MCD
    initialisation (new 'init' argument); the cellwise detection step uses the
    standardised projection test. Default-path results therefore differ from
    earlier development versions.
  + cellPcaCoDa() now requires at least 3 parts (D >= 3) and warns when
    k = D-1, where the residual space is empty and cellwise detection is
    disabled (use k < D-1).
  + cellPcaCoDa() detects period-2 limit cycles in the alternating scheme and
    stops at the stabilised cycle (new 'cycled' flag in the result) instead of
    running to maxiter.
  + ggplot2, pls and data.table moved from 'Depends' to 'Imports' (they are no
    longer attached to the search path; load them explicitly if your own code
    relied on that attachment)

